{"name":"Squeeze Toy Alien","hex":"#11ee00","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"squeeze","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To apply pressure (to something) from two or more sides at once.","To embrace closely; to give a tight hug to."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["An instance of squeezing.","A close or tight fit."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/squeeze"},{"term":"toy","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Symbol","definitions":["ISO 639-3 language code for Topoiyo."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Something to play with, especially as intended for use by a child. .mw-parser-output .defdate{font-size:smaller}","A thing of little importance or value; a trifle."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/toy"},{"term":"alien","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A person, animal, plant, or other thing which is from outside the family, group, organization, or territory under consideration.","A citizen or national of another sovereign state."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Not belonging to the same country, land, or government, or to the citizens or subjects thereof; foreign.","Very unfamiliar, strange, or removed."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/alien"}],"entries":[{"title":"Squeaky toy","blocks":[{"text":"A squeaky toy is a soft, hollow toy made from flexible materials such as rubber or vinyl, and usually equipped with a small device known as a squeaker."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a4/Chonchote.JPG/330px-Chonchote.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Squeaky_toy","wikidata":"Q25220271"},{"title":"Toy","blocks":[{"text":"A toy or plaything is an object that is used primarily to provide entertainment. Simple examples include toy blocks, board games, and dolls. Toys are often designed for use by children, although many are designed specifically for adults and pets. Toys can provide utilitarian benefits, including physical exercise, cultural awareness, or academic education. Additionally, utilitarian objects, especially those which are no longer needed for their original purpose, can be used as toys. Examples include children building a fort with empty cereal boxes and tissue paper spools, or a toddler playing with a broken TV remote. The term \"toy\" can also be used to refer to utilitarian objects purchased for enjoyment rather than need, or for expensive necessities for which a large fraction of the cost represents its ability to provide enjoyment to the owner, such as luxury cars, high-end motorcycles, gaming computers, and flagship smartphones."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c0/Toy_car_%28AM_1996.165.95%29.jpg/330px-Toy_car_%28AM_1996.165.95%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Toy","wikidata":"Q11422"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/ce/Tyrannus_verticalis_4.jpg/500px-Tyrannus_verticalis_4.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/ce/Tyrannus_verticalis_4.jpg/1280px-Tyrannus_verticalis_4.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/ce/Tyrannus_verticalis_4.jpg/500px-Tyrannus_verticalis_4.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A western kingbird","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ATyrannus_verticalis_4.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/15/Little_horse_on_wheels_%28Ancient_greek_child%27s_Toy%29.jpg/500px-Little_horse_on_wheels_%28Ancient_greek_child%27s_Toy%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/15/Little_horse_on_wheels_%